      art (no software-scale jaggies, no aspect stretch); verified headless via Xvfb + x11grab
    ✔ 10 rainbow dice SETS (data-driven) + per-player / per-monster selection, with a live @done(26-07-25)
      SETTINGS preview using the same hardware render
    ✔ Selectable numeral FONT (dicefonts.txt) + hi-res atlas; 1- and 2-digit faces same size @done(26-07-25)
    ✔ Royal-purple tray, per-bounce beeps + settle boop, calmer tumble, longer settle hold @done(26-07-25)
    ✔ Sum revealed beat-by-beat ("3 + 3 + 2 = 8") with the modifier; nat d20 (1/20) skips it @done(26-07-25)
    ✔ 4d6-drop-lowest ability rolls on the 3D dice (module `dl` notation; lowest shrink-fades) @done(26-07-25)
    ✔ FAIRNESS FIX: the die drew its value from the biased physics face (cube-sampled start @done(26-07-25)
      orientation + tip-to-nearest settle). Now a uniform RNG value is drawn and the die is
      posed to show it -- physics is pure animation (d20 mean 10.50, each face ~5.0%).
    ✔ SAVE corruption fix: boolean level-arrays ran together as "-1-1-1-1" (STR$ has no leading @done(26-07-25)
      space for negatives) and desynced the load, leaking save data into the champion's name.
    ✔ Board MARKERS: a fallen-body glyph where an adventurer died and left loot; a $ for treasure @done(26-07-25)
      left to recover (e.g. a curio left unopened). Both clear when the loot is claimed or lost.
    ✔ Upstream DICE3D: ported the HW renderer + fairness + texture fixes back to the module and @done(26-07-25)
      added a [G] software/hardware render toggle to DICE3D-TEST.BAS (grymmjack/qb64 PRs #1, #2).
